{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119174","id":3618008025,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7XpmvZ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119174","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119174/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119174/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119174/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1b98247ef882ce60485c19054e0adfcb5cc4ceb6","number":119174,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix pragma includes","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR accomplishes two things:\r\n* Remove the now unnecessary `#include \"core/object/class_db.h\" // IWYU pragma: keep. ADD_SIGNAL macro.` includes. These are unnecessary since #117474 removed the `ClassDB` dependency for that macro. \r\n  * There's also one other include which I could remove which isn't `class_db.h`, I'm grouping it in this \"one thing\". \r\n* Removes the `using element_type = T` from `RequiredParam`/`RequiredResult` templates. `clangd-tidy`'s include cleaner just doesn't like that. So it's gone, and now it won't trigger unused include warnings, with one narrow exception ([see comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174#issuecomment-4364378370)). \r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Outdated Part 2 </summary>\r\n\r\n* Adds `// IWYU pragma: keep. Used via get_root()` to all of the `window.h` includes, which now need it after #118590. These missing pragmas have been causing a bunch of PR to fail `clangd-tidy` checks for something completely unrelated to their work. \r\n\r\nSome details on 2:\r\nIt appears that `clang`'s `include-cleaner` (which `clangd-tidy` uses) has some issues with templates. In these cases, `RequiredResult<T>`. The pragma is only needed if the following conditions are met:\r\n1. The result of the method which returns `RequiredResult<T>` is never stored as `T` or `T *`\r\n2. The methods called on the result are not `T` methods but methods from `T`'s ancestor classes. \r\n4. Those ancestor classes are included (directly or transitively)\r\n\r\nIn all cases, it's due to `SceneTree::get_singleton()->get_root()` which returns `RequiredResult<Window>`, and then (in most) being directly used for `add_child()` (which is a `Node` method, and `Node` is pretty much universally included) in the form `SceneTree::get_singleton()->get_root()->add_child()`. \r\n</details>","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id